# Normalize every text file to LF, both in the repository and on checkout.
#
# Git already stores LF internally; `eol=lf` additionally forces LF in the
# working tree, so a Windows clone cannot reintroduce CRLF. No tracked file in
# this repository currently contains CRLF, so this is a no-op on existing
# content -- it only pins the behaviour going forward.
#
# `text=auto` still lets Git detect binary content and leave it untouched; the
# explicit `binary` entries below are belt-and-braces for types Git would
# otherwise have to sniff.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Executed directly, so a stray CR breaks the shebang with the notoriously
# opaque "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M".
*.sh        text eol=lf
.githooks/* text eol=lf
